


#### SAS IF vs R IF — One-to-One Mapping
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| SAS IF Condition                           | R Equivalent                          |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IF                                         | `if`                                  |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN                                    | `if { }`                              |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–ELSE                               | `if ... else`                         |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–ELSE IF                            | `if ... else if ... else`             |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–DO                                 | `if { multiple statements }`          |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| ELSE–DO                                    | `else { multiple statements }`        |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Nested IF                                  | Nested `if`                           |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Logical operators (AND, OR, NOT)           | `&&` / `&`, `||` / `|`, `!`           |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Comparison operators (=, >, <, ≥, ≤, NE)   | `==`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `!=`      |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IN operator                                | `%in%`                                |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Missing values (`.` , `" "`)               | `is.na()`                             |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IFN()                                      | `ifelse()` (numeric)                  |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| IFC()                                      | `ifelse()` (character)                |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| SELECT–WHEN                                | `switch()` / `case_when()`            |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| WHERE vs IF                                | Subsetting / logical indexing         |
|--------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|




| SAS IF Condition                         | SAS Example                                   | R Example                                          | Key Point                                   |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IF                                       | `if age > 18;`                                | `if (age > 18) {}`                                | Basic condition check                       |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN                                  | `if score >= 50 then result="Pass";`          | `if (score >= 50) result <- "Pass"`               | Executes when condition is TRUE             |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–ELSE                             | `if score>=50 then r="Pass"; else r="Fail";`  | `if (score>=50) r<-"Pass" else r<-"Fail"`         | Two-way decision                            |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–ELSE IF                          | `if s>=75 then g="A";                         |`if (s>=75) g<-"A"                                 |                                             |
|                                          |  else if s>=60 then g="B";                    | else if (s>=60) g<-"B"                            |                                             | 
|                                          |  else g="C";`                                 | else g<-"C"`                                      |  Multiple conditions                        |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IF–THEN–DO                               | `if d="IT" then do; b=500; t=50; end;`        | `if (d=="IT") { b<-500; t<-50 }`                  | Multiple statements                         |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| ELSE–DO                                  | `if d="IT" then b=500;                        | `if (d=="IT") b<-500                              |                                             |
|                                          |   else do; b=300; t=30;                       | else { b<-300; t<-30 }`                           |                                             |
|                                          |    end;`                                      |                                                   | ELSE block                                  |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Nested IF                                | `if d="IT" then do; if e>5 then l="S"; end;`  | `if (d=="IT") { if (e>5) l<-"S" }`                | IF inside IF                                |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Logical operators                        | `if age>18 and age<60 then s="W";`            | `if (age>18 && age<60) s<-"W"`                    | AND/OR/NOT logic                            |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Comparison operators                     | `if sal ne 0 then t="Y";`                     | `if (sal != 0) t<-"Y"`                            | Value comparison                            |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IN operator                              | `if st in ("CA","TX") then r="US";`           | `if (st %in% c("CA","TX")) r<-"US"`               | Multiple value check                        |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| Missing values                           | `if m=. then s="M";`                          | `if (is.na(m)) s<-"M"`                            | Handle missing data                         |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IFN()                                    | `r=ifn(s>=50,1,0);`                           | `r<-ifelse(s>=50,1,0)`                            | Numeric conditional                         |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| IFC()                                    | `r=ifc(s>=50,"P","F");`                       | `r<-ifelse(s>=50,"P","F")`                        | Character conditional                       |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| SELECT–WHEN                              | `select; when(s>=75) g="A";                   |                                                   |                                             |
                                              otherwise g="C"; end;`                       | `g<-case_when(s>=75~"A", TRUE~"C")`               | Clean alternative to IF–ELSE                |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
| WHERE vs IF                              | `if age>18;`                                  | `df <- df[df$age>18, ]`                            | Row filtering                              |
|------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|
